# RECIPE flyby: the camera flies along a route past a parked car, always looking at it. Copy it, point `path` at your own route file, change the car.
#
# What it uses: a spot for the car (hw-lane1, lane 1 of the street outside the Hollywood garage gate: @0,0,6 is 6 m along it), a route file for the
# CAMERA (routes\street-fly.route, beside this scene: x,z,speed,y waypoints 3 m to the right of lane 1, 50 m, 9 m/s) and `rig flyby` (camera.h): the camera starts
# at the route's first point when the key's time comes, flies at the route's own speeds (`speed 7` = 7 m/s, `speed x0.8` = 0.8 of them), holds at its last
# point, and looks at `track car:p1 <dx> <dy> <dz>` (the point in the car's frame, here the middle of the body 0.7 m up). `up 2.5` is the height above the
# route's own heights; a route with no heights (x,z,speed only) needs `y <metres>` in the world instead.
# A flyby that passes close to a car looks quick: lengthen the route, lower `speed`, or give `aimlag 0.2` so the aim trails a little.
#
# Timeline: the car is ready at about 5 s; the camera starts at 6 and flies 50 m at 8 m/s: 6.3 s; it holds at the end; the game's camera is back at 15.
#   6     the flyby starts at the route's first point, 2.5 m above the road, fov 42
#   10    the lens has zoomed to fov 28 (fov is interpolated in focal length: a zoom looks even); the flyby goes on, a key that names no position leaves it alone
# The camera's position is the route's closed form of the scene time: a scrub and a take give the same place.
scene recipe-flyby fps 60 step 1/60
world hour 17.3 hold weather nice traffic off peds off parked off police off
at 0 hud off
at 0.5 car p1 spawn vp_lam_murcielago_06 at spot:hw-lane1@0,0,6 heading spot:hw-lane1
cam 6 rig flyby path street-fly.route speed 8 up 2.5 track car:p1 0 0.7 0 fov 42
cam 10 fov 28
at 15 mark game-camera
cam 15 off
at 15.5 car p1 delete
end 16.5
